<%#
  The SIMULATED tournament this job ran — every round, step by step, read from
  spec["tournament"] (jobs#create_tournament_job). The SAME rule /tournament
  exists under: the pipeline never picks a winner, and this bracket decides
  nothing — it is a simulation, said so plainly, in the same words the page
  says them.

  The DRAWN BRACKET link posts the field + seed back to /tournament, which
  appends the meme entrant itself and derives the layout from the same
  threshold — so the bracket the page draws is the one this job ran, because
  the whole sim is deterministic in the seed. spec["entrants"] is the FIELD
  (without the meme entrant) for exactly that reason.
%>
<% t = @job.spec["tournament"] %>
<% if t.is_a?(Hash) && t["outcomes"].is_a?(Array) %>
<div class="card process-card">
  <div class="process-head">
    <%= record_section("Tournament") %>
    <span class="process-count mono">
      SIMULATED · <%= t["entrants"].to_a.size + 1 %> entrants ·
      <%= t["rounds"] %> rounds · seed <span class="mono"><%= t["seed"] %></span>
    </span>
  </div>
  <p class="hint">
    A simulation, not a selection: it decides nothing about the pipeline —
    exactly what <a href="<%= tournament_path(entrants: t["entrants"], seed: t["seed"]) %>">/tournament</a>
    says of the same bracket.
    <% if t["prompt"].present? %>The prompt <span class="mono"><%= t["prompt"] %></span>
      is the seed, so re-filing this prompt runs this same tournament.<% end %>
    <% if t["source"] == "memes" %>Entrants drawn from the MET-Meme annotation
      vocabulary (MemeVocabulary).<% end %>
  </p>
  <table class="candidates process-tbl">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th class="col-narrow">#</th>
        <th>Round</th>
        <th>Match</th>
        <th>Winner</th>
        <th>Note</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% t["outcomes"].each_with_index do |o, i| %>
        <tr>
          <td class="col-narrow mono"><%= i + 1 %></td>
          <td class="mono">round <%= o["round"] %></td>
          <td class="mono"><%= o["a"] || "—" %> vs <%= o["b"] || "—" %></td>
          <td class="mono"><%= o["winner"] %></td>
          <td class="mono"><%= o["note"] %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
      <tr>
        <td class="col-narrow mono">★</td>
        <td class="mono" colspan="2">champion (simulated)</td>
        <td class="mono" colspan="2"><%= t["champion"] %></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<% end %>
